{#-
  Spiko tokenized funds (T-Bills MMFs + Smart Cash / SAFO) — INVESTOR side.

  Covers every Spiko share token: the T-Bills money-market funds (EUTBL,
  USTBL) AND the Smart Cash / SAFO classes (eurSAFO, usdSAFO, gbpSAFO,
  chfSAFO — the Spiko Amundi Overnight Swap Fund behind "Spiko Smart Cash").
  All are the same transfer-restricted ERC-20 + ERC-1363 "Token" contract
  redeeming into ONE shared per-chain Redemption contract, so a single
  template + role set covers them uniformly — list whichever keys apply in
  the `funds` param.

  Spiko funds are permissioned, transfer-restricted ERC-20 share tokens.
  There is NO on-chain subscribe/mint for investors: subscription is an
  off-chain fiat / stablecoin deposit followed by an operator-only mint to
  the (KYC-allowlisted) Safe. The ONLY investor-initiated on-chain write is
  redemption, performed via ERC-1363 `transferAndCall` ON THE SHARE TOKEN —
  no prior ERC-20 approve is needed:

    transferAndCall(to = Redemption, value = shares, data = abi.encode(output, salt))

  The token escrows the shares to the shared Redemption contract and logs a
  PENDING request; Spiko's operator later settles the payout to the caller.
  If the operator never settles before the on-chain deadline, anyone — the
  Safe included — may call the permissionless `cancelRedemption` to refund
  the escrowed shares to `user`.

  Each entry in `funds` is a fund alias KEY, resolved via aliases.spiko[<key>]
  with NO existence guard. If the alias is missing on the active chain,
  rendering throws — there is no silent fall-through. To grant the Safe
  redemption of a fund, add the key to `funds` AND ensure the matching entry
  exists in aliases/<chain>/spiko.yaml. Each resolved entry must declare:
    address — the fund's share-token contract (EUTBL / USTBL)

  The shared Redemption contract is canonical-per-chain and is resolved from
  aliases.spiko.redemption.address — NOT passed as a param.

  Required template params:
    funds — list of fund alias keys, e.g. ["eutbl", "ustbl"].
            aliases.spiko[<key>] must exist ⇒ render-time error otherwise.

  Output shape:
    - One role per fund token: redeem via transferAndCall, with `to` pinned to
      the Redemption contract (equal_to). `value` (shares) and `data` (the
      abi-encoded output+salt blob) pass — the on-chain Redemption guard
      enforces that `output` is a Spiko-registered output for this token (on
      the live mainnet contract that output is the zero address — actual
      stablecoin settlement is performed off-chain) and that the caller is
      allowlisted, while pinning `to` guarantees shares can only ever be
      escrowed to the canonical Redemption contract.
    - One role on the Redemption contract: cancelRedemption, with `user`
      pinned to the avatar (refunds can only ever return to the Safe) and
      `input` pinned to the fund(s) in scope.

  NOT emitted (delegated-redemption path): transferFromAndCall / approve /
  permit. Those are only needed when a Spiko relayer redeems on the Safe's
  behalf via an allowance; that flow needs a Spiko-specific spender address
  and is out of scope for this self-service template.
-#}
{%- set redemption = aliases.spiko.redemption -%}
roles:
{%- for key in funds %}
{%- set fund = aliases.spiko[key] %}

  - address: "{{ fund.address }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function transferAndCall(address to, uint256 value, bytes data)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: to
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ redemption.address }}"
            value_type: "address"
          - name: value
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: data
            param_type: "dynamic"
            operator: "pass"
{%- endfor %}

  - address: "{{ redemption.address }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function cancelRedemption(address user, address input, address output, uint256 inputValue, bytes32 salt)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: user
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: input
            param_type: "static"
{%- if funds | length == 1 %}
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ aliases.spiko[funds[0]].address }}"
            value_type: "address"
{%- else %}
            operator: "oneOf"
            values:
{%- for key in funds %}
              - "{{ aliases.spiko[key].address }}"
{%- endfor %}
            value_type: "address"
{%- endif %}
          - name: output
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: inputValue
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: salt
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
